  "slug": "locksmith-job-work-order-form",
  "title": "Locksmith Job Work Order and Key Control",
  "subtitle": "Verify access authority, define the exact opening and credential scope, authorize price limits, control site access, record installed hardware and issued keys, test security and egress, and complete a secure customer handoff.",
  "description": "A workflow-complete locksmith work order covering controlled job identity, customer and property routing, minimum necessary authority verification, requested lock and access-control scope, opening-by-opening requirements, estimates and authorization limits, technician arrival and alarm coordination, completed work and materials, key and credential issuance, old-hardware disposition, functional and egress tests, unresolved security concerns, invoice details, warranty information, and customer acceptance.",
  "use_case": "Use when a dispatcher, locksmith technician, authorized property or vehicle representative, and customer need one fillable record connecting verified access authority and approved security scope to work performed, controlled credential custody, testing, invoice delivery, and accountable release.",
  "risk_tier": "A",
  "sections": [
